observations_revision.description:
The volatile half: every reading this controller takes of something no writer of this lifecycle moves. That is exactly the set `state_revision` leaves out and a reading still turns on, and the list is the definition rather than an illustration of it:

- whether each task admitted into an open round stands complete in `.ai-tasks/`;
- whether the current batch's analysis task stands complete there, which is what tells `batch-frozen` from every stage after it and what the gate verbs are offered from;
- which of a batch's claimed report bundles are staged on this machine;
- what each planned target's deploy receipt holds;
- the age the clock gives the standing offer, since `max_wait_days` past its oldest member has the policy release a batch the same offer needed an argued force for yesterday;
- what this checkout can resolve: the revisions records name and no watched ref holds, so a fetch that moves no tip still settles a release placement or an attempt's ref chain that read unverified an hour ago.

It exists because those readings are not decoration. `seal-round` is allowed exactly when every admitted task of the open round is observed complete, so an allowed-action set moves when a task file does — under a `state_revision` that has not moved and must not, since nothing was written and every mutation re-reads `.ai-tasks/` under the lock anyway. A surface holding one token could not tell a reading that still stands from one whose offered actions have changed underneath it.

It digests the answers and never the inputs they were read from, which is what makes it a token at all. `now` differs at every call and an object store is not a thing that can be enumerated, so a digest over either would move on every reading and guarantee nothing; a digest over a task file's bytes would move for an edit that changed no answer. What is hashed is what the reading made of them — each completion answer, the staged set, each target's state, the admission trigger the age produced, and each placement or chain link this checkout could or could not settle.

What it guarantees is weaker on purpose, and stated so no caller mistakes it for the other: it says this reading was taken over the same observations, and nothing more. It is not a lock, no mutation accepts it, and it moves on its own — a colleague finishing a task in another window moves it, so does deploying a target, and so does the clock passing a threshold nobody touched. A console re-reads on it; it never refuses on it.
